aneous manifestations", "Abnormal rash distribution (face, torso, extremities)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Insulin Resistance Syndromes", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3957240437158469, "posterior": 0.3804237115502139, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The subacute course and hyperglycemia provide strong evidence for beta cell destruction (B2), but systemic symptoms suggest a broader process."], "evidence_against": ["Hyperglycemia moderately supports infectious/inflammatory disease (B6), while normal temperature slightly weakens this possibility."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Beta Cell Destruction in Diabetes", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3299289617486338, "posterior": 0.3171725402322265, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The subacute course and hyperglycemia provide strong evidence for beta cell destruction (B2), but systemic symptoms suggest a broader process."], "evidence_against": ["Systemic symptoms weakly contradict beta cell destruction (B2) as the sole explanation, favoring hyperglycemic tumors (B3) and beta cell tumors (B5)."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Endocrine Tumor with Hyperglycemic Effects", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.18594262295081965, "posterior": 0.17875331024648608, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "e